# State drift watcher (Dan 2026-11-23)

- A scheduled task runs `<Projects>\_tools\state-drift-watch.py --repo <this repo>` on Dan's PC. Each run pulls the workstation repo first (ff-only), so it checks against the latest workstation-core state rules and tools.
- It appends each new finding to the store `BACKLOG.md` as `- [WATCH <key>] <text>` under a dated "state drift watch" heading, and never edits the repo.
- Every agent opening a PR in this repo first reads the open `[WATCH ...]` lines and fixes each one in that PR (or the next one if it does not fit), without asking Dan. It lists them in the PR body on a `Watch:` line, marks each BACKLOG line `[DONE #<PR>]`, and tells Dan in the reply as a note, not a question.
- A finding that would change a SoT data file, the master wire list or SPEC is the exception: it waits for Dan's yes (BACKLOG `needs owner yes`).
- A repo decision beats the template where DECISIONS says so (example: the one-line `CLAUDE.md`, Dan B2 a); the watcher skips those.
- Enforcer: the watcher itself; no gate.
